University of Cincinnati team unexpectedly discovered a large stone-built tomb 
of Late Helladic IIA date near Tholos Tomb IV on the first day of renewed 
excavations at the Palace of Nestor, Pylos. Hundreds of artifacts of gold, 
silver, bronze, ivory, and semiprecious stones were found with the body of a 
single male, 30-35 years old, dubbed the “Griffin Warrior.” Many of the grave 
goods were manufactured in the Minoan world. Among the gold artifacts were four 
