gold, silver, bronze, ivory, and semiprecious stones were found with the body of
a single male, 30-35 years old, dubbed the “Griffin Warrior.” Many of the grave 
goods were manufactured in the Minoan world. Among the gold artifacts were four 
signet rings decorated with Minoan ritual scenes.", "source_ids": 
