editions.[10][20][21] The treasure as presented in his study does not derive 
from a single excavated tomb with secure stratigraphic documentation, but rather
from a collection of objects grouped and interpreted by Evans in the early 20th 
century.[10][20] Subsequent scholarship has therefore treated the ring as 
unprovenanced in strict archaeological terms, even when discussing its possible 
